{"content_hash": "adf3e1270eebc770", "version_id": 693, "article_id": 70, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "France arrests 1,200 as protests turn violent", "title_zh": "法国抗议演变成暴力，1200多人被捕", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6d937wedj7jo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1485504750689-aa2121ffe6c6?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8dmlvbGVudCUyMGNsYXNoZXMlMjBsb290aW5nfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTIyNzkxMjd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Pawel Janiak on Unsplash", "author": "Pawel Janiak", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@pawelj?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/fire-burning-on-the-road-with-high-rise-buildings-during-daytime-photography-49LBMXrY5BE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(36, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(74, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "f2043e6acb50"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-18", "word_count": 194, "reading_minutes": 1.0, "lead": "Violence broke out across France on Saturday during protests about schools and the cost of living. Police arrested at least 1,200 people, and buildings were set on fire in several cities.", "lead_zh": "周六，法国各地因学校和生活成本问题举行的抗议演变成暴力。警方逮捕了至少1200人，多个城市的建筑被纵火焚烧。", "preview": "About 550,000 people took to the streets on Saturday. In Paris, the main march was mostly peaceful in the afternoon. However, as the day wen", "preview_zh": "周六约有55万人走上街头。在巴黎，下午的主要游行基本和平。然而随着时间推移，一些团体点燃火焰并烧毁汽车，包括在共和国广场。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 681, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 69.95, "size_bytes": 420624, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 226, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b1_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 71.65, "size_bytes": 430848, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 226, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/70/en_b1_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b1_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 75.75, "size_bytes": 455472, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 226, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/70/en_b1_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b1_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 65.375, "size_bytes": 393264, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 226, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/70/en_b1_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b1_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 71.225, "size_bytes": 428256, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 226, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/70/en_b1_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@dcbf67c/content/data/versions/693.json", "paragraphs": ["About 550,000 people took to the streets on Saturday. In Paris, the main march was mostly peaceful in the afternoon. However, as the day went on, some groups lit fires and burned cars, including at the Place de la République.", "Riot police used tear gas and water cannon against crowds, and they charged at people with batons. Looting broke out in several cities, and shops were broken into, including an Apple store in Lille.", "In Limoges, a large fire at the town hall caused the roof to partly collapse. In Lyon, the tourist office burned down, which the mayor called a tragedy for the city. A young man in Saint-Étienne lost his hand in a grenade blast.", "Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said 150 police officers were injured. He added that some groups were using the protests as a warm-up for next year's presidential election, and he warned that no one would impose their political agenda through violence.", "Students have protested for weeks over staff shortages and old school buildings. Trade union members and yellow vest groups joined them on Saturday. President Macron said those who broke, attacked and looted would be prosecuted and punished."], "paragraphs_zh": ["周六约有55万人走上街头。在巴黎，下午的主要游行基本和平。然而随着时间推移，一些团体点燃火焰并烧毁汽车，包括在共和国广场。", "防暴警察对人群使用催泪瓦斯和水炮，并用警棍冲向人群。多个城市爆发抢劫，商店被闯入，包括里尔的一家苹果商店。", "在利摩日，市政厅的一场大火导致屋顶部分坍塌。在里昂，旅游局大楼被烧毁，市长称这对该市是一场悲剧。在圣艾蒂安，一名年轻男子在手榴弹爆炸中失去了一只手。", "总理塞巴斯蒂安·勒科尔尼表示，150名警察受伤。他还说，一些团体把抗议当作明年总统选举的热身，并警告没有人能通过暴力强加自己的政治议程。", "学生们因师资短缺和校舍老旧已抗议数周。周六，工会成员和“黄背心”团体也加入了他们。马克龙总统表示，那些破坏、袭击和抢劫的人将被起诉并受到惩罚。"], "body": "About 550,000 people took to the streets on Saturday. In Paris, the main march was mostly peaceful in the afternoon. However, as the day went on, some groups lit fires and burned cars, including at the Place de la République.\n\nRiot police used tear gas and water cannon against crowds, and they charged at people with batons. Looting broke out in several cities, and shops were broken into, including an Apple store in Lille.\n\nIn Limoges, a large fire at the town hall caused the roof to partly collapse. In Lyon, the tourist office burned down, which the mayor called a tragedy for the city. A young man in Saint-Étienne lost his hand in a grenade blast.\n\nPrime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said 150 police officers were injured. He added that some groups were using the protests as a warm-up for next year's presidential election, and he warned that no one would impose their political agenda through violence.\n\nStudents have protested for weeks over staff shortages and old school buildings. Trade union members and yellow vest groups joined them on Saturday. President Macron said those who broke, attacked and looted would be prosecuted and punished.", "body_zh": "周六约有55万人走上街头。在巴黎，下午的主要游行基本和平。然而随着时间推移，一些团体点燃火焰并烧毁汽车，包括在共和国广场。\n\n防暴警察对人群使用催泪瓦斯和水炮，并用警棍冲向人群。多个城市爆发抢劫，商店被闯入，包括里尔的一家苹果商店。\n\n在利摩日，市政厅的一场大火导致屋顶部分坍塌。在里昂，旅游局大楼被烧毁，市长称这对该市是一场悲剧。在圣艾蒂安，一名年轻男子在手榴弹爆炸中失去了一只手。\n\n总理塞巴斯蒂安·勒科尔尼表示，150名警察受伤。他还说，一些团体把抗议当作明年总统选举的热身，并警告没有人能通过暴力强加自己的政治议程。\n\n学生们因师资短缺和校舍老旧已抗议数周。周六，工会成员和“黄背心”团体也加入了他们。马克龙总统表示，那些破坏、袭击和抢劫的人将被起诉并受到惩罚。", "text": "About 550,000 people took to the streets on Saturday. In Paris, the main march was mostly peaceful in the afternoon. However, as the day went on, some groups lit fires and burned cars, including at the Place de la République. Riot police used tear gas and water cannon against crowds, and they charged at people with batons. Looting broke out in several cities, and shops were broken into, including an Apple store in Lille. In Limoges, a large fire at the town hall caused the roof to partly collapse. In Lyon, the tourist office burned down, which the mayor called a tragedy for the city. A young man in Saint-Étienne lost his hand in a grenade blast. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said 150 police officers were injured. He added that some groups were using the protests as a warm-up for next year's presidential election, and he warned that no one would impose their political agenda through violence. Students have protested for weeks over staff shortages and old school buildings. Trade union members and yellow vest groups joined them on Saturday. President Macron said those who broke, attacked and looted would be prosecuted and punished.", "vocab": [{"word": "break out", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "爆发", "note": "常指暴力、火灾、疾病等突然发生", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "arrest", "pos": "verb", "zh": "逮捕", "note": "be arrested 表示“被捕”", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "protest", "pos": "noun", "zh": "抗议", "note": "也可作动词，protest against 表示“抗议某事”", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "looting", "pos": "noun", "zh": "抢劫；趁乱打劫", "note": "动词原形为 loot", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "riot police", "pos": "noun", "zh": "防暴警察", "note": "处理骚乱的专门警力", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "tear gas", "pos": "noun", "zh": "催泪瓦斯", "note": "不可数名词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "collapse", "pos": "verb", "zh": "坍塌", "note": "建筑物倒塌常用此词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "injure", "pos": "verb", "zh": "使受伤", "note": "be injured 表示“受伤”", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "prosecute", "pos": "verb", "zh": "起诉", "note": "法律用语，指正式起诉某人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "cost of living", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "生活成本", "note": "常见新闻话题词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-10-17T23:18:45.972331", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "About", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.55, "sm": 275, "em": 550, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "550,000", "s": 0.55, "e": 1.775, "sm": 550, "em": 1774, "cs": 6, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "people", "s": 1.775, "e": 2.15, "sm": 1775, "em": 2150, "cs": 14, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "took", "s": 2.15, "e": 2.325, "sm": 2150, "em": 2324, "cs": 21, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "to", "s": 2.325, "e": 2.412, "sm": 2325, "em": 2412, "cs": 26, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "the", "s": 2.413, "e": 2.5, "sm": 2412, "em": 2499, "cs": 29, "ce": 32, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "streets", "s": 2.5, "e": 2.837, "sm": 2500, "em": 2837, "cs": 33, "ce": 40, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "on", "s": 2.837, "e": 3.025, "sm": 2837, "em": 3025, "cs": 41, "ce": 43, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "Saturday", "s": 3.025, "e": 3.875, "sm": 3025, "em": 3875, "cs": 44, "ce": 52, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": ".", "s": 3.875, "e": 4.037, "sm": 3875, "em": 4037, "cs": 52, "ce": 53, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "In", "s": 4.037, "e": 4.175, "sm": 4037, "em": 4175, "cs": 54, "ce": 56, "si": 1}, {"i": 11, "w": "Paris", "s": 4.175, "e": 4.775, "sm": 4175, "em": 4774, "cs": 57, "ce": 62, "si": 1}, {"i": 12, "w": ",", "s": 4.775, "e": 4.85, "sm": 4775, "em": 4849, "cs": 6